{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai electronic waste ai electronic waste","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md","fileName":"AI Electronic Waste.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Electronic Waste","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Labor and Environmental Ethics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Labor and Environmental Ethics","Sustainable AI","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai electronic waste ai electronic waste","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md","fileName":"AI Electronic Waste.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Electronic Waste","heading":"AI Electronic Waste","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"AI electronic waste is discarded hardware produced as intelligent systems depend on and accelerate replacement of devices, sensors, servers, and other computing equipment. The environmental burden includes raw-material extraction, manufacturing energy, toxic substances, transport, and disposal.\n\nWaste is easy to omit when AI is described only as an algorithm or online service. A sociotechnical view follows the material infrastructure and asks where obsolete equipment goes and who handles it. [[Sustainable AI]] therefore includes durability, maintenance, reuse, and production impacts as well as efficient model operation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Labor and Environmental Ethics","Sustainable AI","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Electronic Waste.md::2","so